The HOKA Arahi SR shoes are stability shoes—meaning they help correct slight overpronation—with a slip-resistant tread for better grip on wet surfaces. Like the HOKA Bondi SRs, the Arahi SRs are a great option for restaurant/bar workers, food delivery workers, healthcare workers, and anyone who might frequently encounter slick surfaces.

You’d want to opt for the Arahi SR over the Bondi SR if your feet overpronate and if you want some additional arch support. If you aren't sure if you overpronate, check with a running specialist or medical professional to analyze your gait.

One of our men’s testers works long shifts at a hospital and found he preferred the HOKA Arahi SRs over the HOKA Bondi SRs because they were more agile and less clunky-feeling. The only reason we didn’t name them the best overall is because they’re stability shoes, designed to help limit overpronation. However, our testers with average arches didn’t find the arch support to be too aggressive, so if you want a pair of slip-resistant walking shoes that are less bulky than the Bondi SRs, this is a worthwhile option.

